---
export const prerender = true;
import MarketingLayout from "@/layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
import Prose from "@/components/marketing/Prose.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Office Ledger collects, uses, stores and protects workspace data."
>
  <Prose
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy policy"
    updated="October 5, 2026"
    lead="Office Ledger processes workplace data on behalf of the organizations that use it. This page explains what we store and why."
  >
    <h2>Who controls the data</h2>
    <p>
      Each workspace is controlled by its organization owner (the "controller"). Office Ledger acts as a
      processor and only uses workspace data to provide the service.
    </p>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account details: name, email address and password hash (Argon2id).</li>
      <li>
        Membership details your organization adds: employee ID, department, designation, joining date and
        contact details.
      </li>
      <li>
        Work records: attendance check-ins and check-outs, leave requests, tasks, meetings, complaints and
        their history.
      </li>
      <li>
        Technical data: session cookies, IP address and browser user agent for security and sign-in
        management.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      To run the features your workspace uses, send the notifications and emails you've opted into, keep
      accounts secure (rate limiting, lockout, audit log) and support you when you ask.
    </p>
    <h2>Location checks</h2>
    <p>
      If your workspace turns on office check-in verification, your browser's location is used only at the
      moment you check in and is never tracked in the background.
    </p>
    <h2>Retention and export</h2>
    <p>
      Data stays until the workspace owner deletes it or the workspace is deleted. Owners can export all
      workspace data as CSV files at any time.
    </p>
    <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
    <p>
      Workspaces are isolated with database row-level security. Private files are stored outside the public
      web root and served only through signed links that expire after a few minutes. Report vulnerabilities
      via our <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Ask your organization owner to access, correct or delete your information, or contact us at{" "}
      <a href="/contact">our contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</MarketingLayout>
